WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:06.923
[intriguing music playing]

00:08.008 --> 00:09.509
[bleak music playing]

00:21.771 --> 00:24.691
MEETING IN THE RAIN

00:24.774 --> 00:28.194
- [grunting]
- [pained yelling]

00:33.283 --> 00:35.744
[shrieking, delighted laughter]

00:38.788 --> 00:40.123
[bird hooting ominously]

00:44.544 --> 00:46.087
[corpse squelching]

00:49.382 --> 00:50.216
Huh?

00:53.887 --> 00:54.971
[music fades]

00:55.805 --> 00:58.475
[Kasukabe] No matter how many times
you come to me, it's pointless.

00:58.558 --> 01:01.603
I won't be able to
turn you into a Sorcerer.

01:02.103 --> 01:04.981
I'm pretty sure that's not
what the book was about either...

01:06.900 --> 01:08.485
That thing wrapped up in the back seat,

01:08.568 --> 01:12.864
it's the corpse of the Sorcerer killed
by the neighborhood association, right?

01:13.782 --> 01:15.617
[Kasukabe] It's for research.

01:18.203 --> 01:19.370
But what's more,

01:19.454 --> 01:22.123
it could help us
to better treat victims of Magic.

01:26.211 --> 01:27.378
[gasps]

01:27.462 --> 01:28.963
[eerie music playing]

01:29.047 --> 01:31.883
[Ai] Are these... all Sorcerers?

01:31.966 --> 01:37.514
Yeah. I secretly collect the Sorcerers
killed by the neighborhood association.

01:38.223 --> 01:40.225
You know, the name Kasukabe

01:41.059 --> 01:42.894
sounds like a Sorcerer's name.

01:43.728 --> 01:46.231
[Kasukabe] Actually,
my wife was a Sorcerer.

01:46.731 --> 01:48.525
But when she fell ill,

01:48.608 --> 01:51.152
I tried to find
anything I could do to help her.

01:51.236 --> 01:54.405
And that's how I ended up
studying Sorcerers here.

01:54.489 --> 01:57.242
[Ai] So, your wife was a Sorcerer.

01:57.742 --> 02:00.453
Yes, but she basically disowned me.

02:00.537 --> 02:04.457
When I released my first book,
I published under my wife's name.

02:04.541 --> 02:06.668
So tell me, what about your folks?

02:06.751 --> 02:10.046
Are they both okay
with you being out in the night?

02:10.672 --> 02:15.176
I have my grandpa, but he's out peddling
and rarely comes home.

02:15.844 --> 02:18.179
[Kasukabe] Why do you want
to become a Sorcerer so badly?

02:18.263 --> 02:19.931
THE HOLE WEST OCTOBER 11TH DEVIL TUMOR

02:20.515 --> 02:22.517
[frantic electronic music playing]

02:34.904 --> 02:37.282
[lyrics in Japanese]

03:48.019 --> 03:49.938
THE BEGINNING

03:52.523 --> 03:54.317
[machine beeping rhythmically]

03:54.400 --> 03:55.443
[Kasukabe sighs]

03:55.526 --> 03:57.528
That's the last one. Next is--

03:57.612 --> 03:58.446
[gasps]

03:59.155 --> 04:00.949
[machine beeping frantically]

04:01.032 --> 04:03.952
[steady beep]

04:04.786 --> 04:06.287
[shocked gasping]

04:06.788 --> 04:12.210
[men chanting] Homage to Amida Buddha.
Homage to Amida Buddha.

04:12.293 --> 04:15.713
- Homage to Amida Buddha. Homage...
- [bell dings]

04:15.797 --> 04:17.799
[Kasukabe] Even with treatment,

04:17.882 --> 04:22.178
the human body cannot withstand
the sudden changes caused by Magic.

04:22.804 --> 04:25.723
In the end,
most patients suddenly die like that.

04:27.225 --> 04:30.603
Is it simply futile,
what I'm trying to do?

04:31.437 --> 04:33.731
Or maybe I'm just...

04:33.815 --> 04:35.275
[bell dings]

04:35.358 --> 04:39.737
The deceased was killed by Magic, right?
Did you fill in the plate properly?

04:42.323 --> 04:45.493
[Ai] Take this medicine in the morning
and at night after meals.

04:45.576 --> 04:47.620
- All right.
- [Ai] Have a nice day.

04:47.704 --> 04:50.832
[Kasukabe] Hey, Ai.
I think it's time for a lunch break.

04:52.375 --> 04:56.754
Sometimes, I wonder if this sky
is connected to the Magic world.

04:56.838 --> 04:59.090
Missing your wife again, are ya?

04:59.173 --> 05:00.258
[chuckling]

05:00.341 --> 05:04.637
You know, it's already been a year
since you started helping me here, Ai.

05:07.098 --> 05:11.311
What are you always doing,
holed up in the laboratory after work?

05:11.811 --> 05:14.439
Perhaps you still haven't given up, huh?

05:14.939 --> 05:16.691
[Kasukabe slurping]

05:18.735 --> 05:22.030
Why is it you want
to become a Sorcerer so badly?

05:23.614 --> 05:25.533
You already asked me that question.

05:26.326 --> 05:29.120
That's 'cause I'm still waiting
for an answer.

05:31.164 --> 05:34.834
Down here in the Hole,
sorry bastards like us are easy prey.

05:35.335 --> 05:37.253
Maybe you can't stand it?

05:38.046 --> 05:42.300
[Ai] You're helping victims of Magic.
Isn't that what keeps you going?

05:43.926 --> 05:46.804
Actually, I'm not that kind of person.

05:47.847 --> 05:49.265
[Ai] Well, for me...

05:54.729 --> 05:57.732
I can't find a reason
to live in this town.

05:59.400 --> 06:00.485
[Kasukabe] We gotta hurry!

06:00.568 --> 06:04.072
I heard the neighborhood association
just threw a Sorcerer into the waste lake!

06:04.155 --> 06:05.698
[tense music playing]

06:07.241 --> 06:09.827
- [gasps] He's so far out!
- [panicked grunting]

06:12.163 --> 06:14.374
This lake is
an extremely dangerous mixture

06:14.457 --> 06:18.586
of raw sewage, wastewater,
and the corpses of many dead Sorcerers.

06:19.379 --> 06:21.506
There's no way we can lift him out.

06:22.173 --> 06:23.674
This one's hopeless.

06:24.675 --> 06:25.676
Ai!

06:26.260 --> 06:27.345
[music fades]

06:27.428 --> 06:28.888
[haunting music playing]

06:28.971 --> 06:30.848
- [Ai coughing]
- [Kasukabe] Ai!

06:30.932 --> 06:32.642
Please, hang in there!

06:32.725 --> 06:34.852
[Ai splutters, wheezes]

06:34.936 --> 06:37.814
[Kasukabe] The water from the lake
has dissolved his flesh

06:37.897 --> 06:39.357
and reached his organs.

06:40.024 --> 06:42.860
- I'm already too...
- [Ai coughing wheezily]

06:43.903 --> 06:45.863
- [weakly] Professor...
- What, Ai?

06:46.531 --> 06:48.866
Get my notebook. [labored breathing]

06:48.950 --> 06:50.201
Look inside.

06:51.828 --> 06:55.039
No way. You're giving this to me?

06:55.123 --> 06:56.457
[Ai] One more corpse...

06:57.583 --> 07:01.879
With one more Sorcerer's corpse,
we can perform that surgery.

07:03.506 --> 07:05.216
Professor, please.

07:05.716 --> 07:09.011
If there's no hope, and I'm going to die,

07:09.095 --> 07:12.765
then at least
I can die with a Sorcerer's body.

07:17.019 --> 07:18.312
All right, Ai

07:19.147 --> 07:24.110
If I can take even just a little
of your despair and turn it into hope...

07:24.193 --> 07:25.361
[relieved sigh]

07:26.988 --> 07:29.407
[saw whirring]

07:29.490 --> 07:30.908
[rhythmic beeping]

07:31.617 --> 07:32.910
[saw whirring]

07:34.036 --> 07:35.788
[Kasukabe] Am I insane?

07:37.874 --> 07:40.918
Doing a make-believe surgery like this...

07:46.007 --> 07:48.050
DAY 1

07:48.134 --> 07:50.178
[Kasukabe] It's a miracle you survived.

07:50.261 --> 07:53.723
I think we'll still have to do
several minor surgeries,

07:53.806 --> 07:58.686
but as long as your body keeps on healing,
I would like to keep a record of it.

08:01.189 --> 08:05.818
I wonder if there's a chance that surgery
really turned him into a Sorcerer.

08:07.153 --> 08:09.697
No, that's impossible...

08:10.364 --> 08:13.701
Human hands aren't capable
of creating Sorcerers.

08:13.784 --> 08:15.203
DAY 201

08:21.042 --> 08:23.961
KASUKABE'S CLINIC

08:24.879 --> 08:26.464
- [Ai] Professor.
- Hm?

08:26.547 --> 08:29.008
[Ai] Um,
now that I can finally walk again,

08:29.091 --> 08:31.469
I'd like to try going outside for a bit.

08:32.011 --> 08:34.972
Of course. A walk will clear your head.

08:39.936 --> 08:44.023
I was thinking, Professor,
back when I fell into that lake,

08:44.524 --> 08:47.860
and I felt the mud and sludge
clinging heavily to my body,

08:47.944 --> 08:52.073
it was like
I was becoming part of the Hole.

08:52.949 --> 08:56.160
At that point,
once I crawled out of there,

08:56.244 --> 08:58.454
I knew for sure I was reborn.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.374
Professor Kasukabe,

09:02.124 --> 09:04.627
I became a Sorcerer.

09:10.508 --> 09:11.634
[Kasukabe] The next day,

09:12.593 --> 09:15.471
Ai's corpse was discovered in the street.

09:16.722 --> 09:17.932
THE PRESENT

09:18.683 --> 09:21.143
[Kasukabe] Ai's body wasn't
in his grave site,

09:21.227 --> 09:25.147
which means
there are two different possibilities.

09:25.231 --> 09:26.732
[keyboard keys clicking]

09:26.816 --> 09:31.153
I found some documents, Mr. Kasukabe.
These are from, like, 13 years ago.

09:31.237 --> 09:35.825
Ai Coleman, plate number 96925.

09:35.908 --> 09:37.159
This number is...

09:37.243 --> 09:39.161
[sizzling]

09:39.245 --> 09:40.997
I can't believe I have to eat lunch

09:41.080 --> 09:44.041
with the people who disturbed
my grandson's resting place.

09:44.625 --> 09:45.960
Yeah, we dug up his grave,

09:46.043 --> 09:48.087
but it's not like
his body was there, right?

09:48.170 --> 09:50.798
[Coleman] That's another thing
I want you to tell me!

09:50.881 --> 09:53.843
- Where did my grandson's corpse go, huh?!
- [shrieking]

09:54.760 --> 09:57.305
- [Vaux] Ah, Professor!
- [Kasukabe] Sorry for the wait!

09:57.388 --> 09:58.931
Where'd you go off to?

09:59.015 --> 10:01.601
The Hole neighborhood association.

10:01.684 --> 10:04.312
The records show
his plate was never collected.

10:04.395 --> 10:08.316
But the wax figure that I saw
in the house was Ai for sure.

10:08.399 --> 10:10.318
What?! What happened to my grandson?!

10:10.401 --> 10:13.696
Ai... So that's the poor bastards name.

10:13.779 --> 10:16.157
Mr. Coleman, you wouldn't know this,

10:16.240 --> 10:20.328
but years ago, I did a surgery on Ai
to turn him into a Sorcerer.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.579
Huh? You what?!

10:21.662 --> 10:23.581
Watch the volume, Grandpa!

10:23.664 --> 10:27.752
- So that's what the file was about...
- [Kasukabe] Look, Mr. Coleman.

10:27.835 --> 10:30.838
Ai might still be alive
in the world of the Sorcerers.

10:30.921 --> 10:32.548
[gasps] What the hell?

10:32.632 --> 10:34.050
Choke on that for a while.

10:35.176 --> 10:38.596
[Kasukabe] I intend to go to the world
of the Sorcerers one more time

10:38.679 --> 10:39.722
to look for Ai.

10:39.805 --> 10:43.059
Well, there's no way I'm going.
No way in hell!

10:43.559 --> 10:45.186
All right, just so you know,

10:45.686 --> 10:49.482
Noi and I are planning to kill
the Cross-Eyes' Boss when we find him.

10:49.565 --> 10:51.984
Yeah, I'm aware of that.

10:52.068 --> 10:54.278
- [dramatic music playing]
- [thunder rumbling]

10:54.362 --> 10:55.988
Looks like it's gonna rain.

10:56.072 --> 10:56.989
STOMACH HELL ALLEY

10:57.073 --> 10:58.741
[Shin] We should get moving, Noi.

10:58.824 --> 11:00.368
Thanks for the food.

11:00.451 --> 11:02.745
But if you take off,
who's going to pay the bill?

11:04.080 --> 11:05.998
[people screaming] A Sorcerer!

11:06.082 --> 11:08.834
Listen, you can come with us,
but this time around,

11:08.918 --> 11:11.295
you're going to have to
look after yourself.

11:11.379 --> 11:13.005
You can't rely on me, okay?

11:13.089 --> 11:14.632
- [Kasukabe gasps]
- [grunts]

11:14.715 --> 11:18.135
Bye, Vaux.
Take care of the bill for me, will you?

11:18.219 --> 11:20.721
Don't expect me back anytime soon.

11:20.805 --> 11:22.139
It's a miracle!

11:22.223 --> 11:23.307
[Kasukabe] Right!

11:24.266 --> 11:27.144
Bye, Mr. Coleman.
I'll let you know if I find Ai.

11:27.228 --> 11:29.146
- [Jonson snarling]
- [Kasukabe] Jonson?!

11:29.230 --> 11:31.440
- [Jonson snarling]
- [yelling]

11:32.108 --> 11:33.401
[music fades]

11:34.110 --> 11:37.029
[gasps] You mean
they were Sorcerers this entire time?

11:37.113 --> 11:39.198
[Vaux] Jeez! What's the matter now, huh?

11:39.281 --> 11:40.199
Well, excuse me!

11:40.282 --> 11:44.245
Maybe I'm cranky because this damn neck
makes swallowing any food take forever!

11:46.372 --> 11:47.832
TRAVEL COMPANIONS

11:47.915 --> 11:49.875
My name is Ebisu.

11:49.959 --> 11:52.795
I was attacked in the Hole
by a man with a lizard face,

11:52.878 --> 11:55.005
and I lost sight of who I really was.

11:55.506 --> 11:57.383
But thanks to En's strange mushrooms,

11:57.466 --> 12:01.554
I remembered my parents
and was able to return to my true self...

12:02.138 --> 12:04.598
I can finally go home.

12:04.682 --> 12:06.809
Life at En's house may have been brutal,

12:07.435 --> 12:08.978
but I have no regrets.

12:09.061 --> 12:10.020
However...

12:10.104 --> 12:11.063
[Fujita] Crap!

12:11.147 --> 12:13.149
- [intriguing music playing]
- [train slowing]

12:13.232 --> 12:16.569
I had some free time,
so I thought I'd see you off!

12:18.863 --> 12:20.573
What? Nothing to say?

12:20.656 --> 12:23.492
[Ebisu] I don't say anything unnecessary.

12:23.576 --> 12:26.412
I am a calm and silent Sorcerer.

12:26.912 --> 12:28.497
- Idiot!
- [Ebisu] Loser!

12:28.581 --> 12:29.707
[Fujita gasps]

12:29.790 --> 12:31.292
Wait up! [groans]

12:31.375 --> 12:34.170
[conductor] Um, please refrain
from rushing onto the train.

12:34.253 --> 12:36.297
It is extremely dangerous.

12:37.465 --> 12:40.050
I believe you just tried to ditch me.

12:40.134 --> 12:43.179
[Ebisu] Rats, I can't go home
looking like this.

12:43.262 --> 12:45.389
I have to change my clothes somewhere...

12:45.473 --> 12:48.309
- [conductor] Next stop, Aridani. Aridani...
- What is she thinking right now?

12:48.392 --> 12:50.311
[train beeping]

12:50.394 --> 12:51.228
[yelps]

12:53.439 --> 12:55.107
Wait, you idiot!

12:56.776 --> 12:58.861
[groans] The bathroom, huh?

12:58.944 --> 13:03.616
[Ebisu] But I didn't bring
any good clothes with me from En's place...

13:04.575 --> 13:08.120
The me my parents know
is a super normal, cute girl,

13:08.204 --> 13:11.207
so they'll get angry at me
if I go like this.

13:11.707 --> 13:13.501
This dress I bought...

13:14.001 --> 13:16.629
Thanks to Fujita,
it's put together all wrong.

13:16.712 --> 13:18.631
There's underwear that doesn't fit,

13:18.714 --> 13:20.883
a bone dress that doesn't cover underwear,

13:20.966 --> 13:23.886
Fujita's lame clothes
from our trip to Hole...

13:23.969 --> 13:26.263
That strange uniform
is out of the question.

13:27.264 --> 13:28.599
Oh...

13:35.606 --> 13:36.774
[music ends abruptly]

13:36.857 --> 13:39.652
Hmph. To hell with the clothes, who cares?

13:39.735 --> 13:42.238
I've been a missing person
this entire time.

13:42.321 --> 13:45.616
I know that Mom and Dad
will just be happy I'm home.

13:46.116 --> 13:49.703
You took your time.
Let me guess, diarrhea again?

13:49.787 --> 13:51.288
- No! Oh!
- Oh.

13:51.372 --> 13:52.832
[laughing smugly]

13:52.915 --> 13:54.542
I finally got you to talk.

13:58.128 --> 14:01.048
[Ebisu] I have to get rid
of this guy somehow.

14:01.131 --> 14:03.717
Maybe I should ask
the friends at Black Tent to lend a hand.

14:03.801 --> 14:04.635
Huh?!

14:04.718 --> 14:06.887
[electronic music pumping in distance]

14:06.971 --> 14:10.391
It's so loud in here!
Is this seriously your house?!

14:10.474 --> 14:13.894
It's just like I thought it'd be.
Your family's a mess.

14:13.978 --> 14:15.646
- [Ebisu] Hey!
- [bartender] Huh?

14:15.729 --> 14:18.274
Aren't you Ebisu? It's been a while.

14:18.357 --> 14:19.859
- [whispering]
- [bartender] Huh?

14:19.942 --> 14:23.362
You're being followed by a strange guy?
Head through the back exit.

14:23.445 --> 14:24.864
Oda will show you the way.

14:25.364 --> 14:28.284
I'm Oda. I'll take you to the exit.

14:28.367 --> 14:31.036
[Ebisu] Who is this guy?
Never seen his face before.

14:31.620 --> 14:34.456
What's this place? Isn't this your house?

14:35.207 --> 14:36.584
Ah! Wait!

14:37.334 --> 14:38.335
Crap!

14:38.419 --> 14:39.753
Hey, open up!

14:39.837 --> 14:41.839
Hey, you're Ebisu, ain't that right?

14:41.922 --> 14:45.342
You got any black powder?
You can't get it anywhere these days.

14:45.926 --> 14:47.344
[Ebisu] Black powder...

14:47.428 --> 14:51.765
[chuckles] I get it, I get it.
You won't tell a newbie like me, right?

14:51.849 --> 14:53.100
[Ebisu] That's right.

14:53.809 --> 14:55.603
[cicadas chirping]

14:58.314 --> 15:00.733
[Ebisu] I can't believe it. I'm back home!

15:03.819 --> 15:06.113
Mom and Dad will be so surprised...

15:06.196 --> 15:07.740
[girl] Coming!

15:08.782 --> 15:10.200
Who are you?

15:10.284 --> 15:12.536
- [Ebisu gasping]
- [uneasy music playing]

15:12.620 --> 15:14.038
[Ebisu] Who are you?

15:14.538 --> 15:16.540
[girl] My name is Ebisu.

15:18.542 --> 15:19.710
[Ebisu] You're lying...

15:19.793 --> 15:21.712
You're lying! I'm Ebisu, not you.

15:21.795 --> 15:23.213
Me, you idiot!

15:23.297 --> 15:25.716
Dad! Mom! [panting]

15:32.473 --> 15:34.266
Where are they?

15:34.350 --> 15:36.143
- [girl] Dad and Mom aren't here.
- [gasps]

15:36.226 --> 15:39.396
They went to work
and haven't come back since.

15:39.480 --> 15:40.731
[Ebisu groans softly]

15:41.231 --> 15:42.650
[girl] Who are you?

15:42.733 --> 15:45.527
I told you, I'm Ebisu,
the daughter of this family!

15:45.611 --> 15:46.904
Who the heck are you?!!

15:49.114 --> 15:51.492
But I'm also Ebisu.

15:51.992 --> 15:55.329
[Ebisu] The same face... as me?

15:55.412 --> 15:56.455
[music fades]

15:56.997 --> 15:58.457
[Ebisu] A doppelgänger!

15:58.540 --> 16:00.417
- [screaming]
- [unsettling music playing]

16:01.543 --> 16:02.920
Huh?

16:03.003 --> 16:04.922
- [Ebisu panting]
- [doppelgänger] Wait.

16:06.006 --> 16:08.175
[Ebisu screaming, panting]

16:10.094 --> 16:11.220
[gasps]

16:11.303 --> 16:12.388
[music fades]

16:14.515 --> 16:17.393
It should be okay
now that she's passed us by.

16:17.476 --> 16:18.644
Nanny!

16:18.727 --> 16:21.897
The young mistress.
You're alive, after all.

16:21.981 --> 16:23.899
- Nanny!
- Ah...

16:23.983 --> 16:27.695
The poor young mistress.
You've really come back home.

16:27.778 --> 16:29.154
But where's Mom and Dad?

16:29.238 --> 16:32.408
[nanny] Since you went missing
all that time ago,

16:32.491 --> 16:35.911
they have both become
more and more closed off.

16:36.620 --> 16:41.875
Around then, your father invited
a shady Sorcerer to the mansion.

16:42.376 --> 16:44.378
[Sorcerer] My Magic is so advanced

16:44.461 --> 16:47.172
that it shortens your life span
each time you use it.

16:47.256 --> 16:49.800
It's a high cost. Are you certain?

16:49.883 --> 16:53.303
Please, I'll pay anything.
Save our daughter!

16:53.387 --> 16:55.556
This is her hair.

16:55.639 --> 17:00.310
[Sorcerer] All right, then.
Now, put that hair into my forehead.

17:00.894 --> 17:02.062
[strained grunting]

17:02.146 --> 17:03.063
Uh, yes!

17:05.649 --> 17:07.651
[muffled grunting]

17:15.534 --> 17:18.454
Now open the cap and squeeze!

17:18.537 --> 17:19.830
[both hesitating] Yes!

17:19.913 --> 17:21.498
[both straining]

17:23.417 --> 17:25.836
[fearful gasping]

17:25.919 --> 17:27.838
[Sorcerer] Now keep it coming!

17:27.921 --> 17:30.340
- [eerie music playing]
- [both straining]

17:40.934 --> 17:43.604
[strained grunting]

17:46.607 --> 17:48.484
[intriguing music playing]

17:53.363 --> 17:55.032
[both gasping]

17:57.159 --> 17:59.536
[nanny] That thing is what came out.

17:59.620 --> 18:03.540
Although your father doted on her
in the beginning,

18:03.624 --> 18:05.918
after all, she looks just like you,

18:06.001 --> 18:09.421
but deep down,
her true nature was something unfamiliar.

18:09.505 --> 18:14.843
Your mom and dad became scared,
left the mansion, and escaped...

18:16.595 --> 18:17.721
[gasping]

18:17.805 --> 18:19.848
Nanny, you burnt the cookies.

18:19.932 --> 18:23.936
You destroyed my precious cookies,
so, Nanny, you're fired!

18:24.019 --> 18:24.853
Huh?

18:24.937 --> 18:26.355
[Ebisu gasping]

18:26.438 --> 18:28.857
You have the same face as me.

18:29.775 --> 18:30.859
I get it.

18:30.943 --> 18:34.488
You're nothing but a fake me!

18:34.571 --> 18:36.406
[fearful gasping]

18:37.491 --> 18:39.201
[screaming, grunts]

18:39.701 --> 18:40.828
[dramatic music playing]

18:40.911 --> 18:43.330
[demonic laughter]

18:43.413 --> 18:45.457
That thing is gonna kill me.

18:45.541 --> 18:48.085
[maniacal demonic laughter continues]

18:51.839 --> 18:54.133
[Ebisu breathing shakily]

18:57.177 --> 18:58.846
[grunts, panting]

18:59.930 --> 19:02.558
[straining]

19:07.437 --> 19:09.857
[laughing maniacally]

19:11.441 --> 19:12.734
[gasps]

19:12.818 --> 19:14.903
- There's only two bags.
- [music softens]

19:14.987 --> 19:16.738
[laughing]

19:20.242 --> 19:22.119
[roaring]

19:22.202 --> 19:23.745
[dramatic music playing]

19:26.832 --> 19:28.041
[groaning]

19:28.125 --> 19:30.419
[laughing]

19:31.336 --> 19:33.881
[guttural growling, snarling]

19:37.342 --> 19:38.552
[music fades]

19:39.845 --> 19:42.181
[woman] Hey, I got an order
for three more meals!

19:42.264 --> 19:43.265
FINAL NIGHT FOR TWO

19:43.348 --> 19:45.767
Jeez, there are so many customers today!

19:45.851 --> 19:49.855
Come on, let's get moving!
Hurry up, you part-timers!

19:50.355 --> 19:52.691
[Tetsujo] Damn lady
is working us like dogs!

19:52.774 --> 19:54.151
[Dokuga] Just deal with it.

19:54.234 --> 19:57.613
We may not pay rent anymore,
but we still need money to eat.

19:58.113 --> 20:00.657
[Ton] Ooh, it looks delicious.

20:00.741 --> 20:03.035
[Ushishimada] It's a cruel job.

20:03.118 --> 20:06.205
Our boss is coming back soon.
Just be patient.

20:06.288 --> 20:08.290
[woman] What are you snacking on?!

20:08.373 --> 20:10.292
MAGMA BATH

20:15.130 --> 20:18.967
I was friends with Risu,
and we went to that school together.

20:19.593 --> 20:21.970
He knows my true identity.

20:23.847 --> 20:26.266
What is this uneasiness I feel?

20:26.975 --> 20:28.310
[sighs contemplatively]

20:28.393 --> 20:29.728
[Natsuki sighs happily]

20:29.811 --> 20:32.314
I hope I get to see the boss.

20:32.397 --> 20:34.524
What's the boss like anyway?

20:34.608 --> 20:36.610
Oh, he's a really strong guy.

20:36.693 --> 20:40.447
He's a savior to those like the rest of us
who can't use any Magic!

20:40.530 --> 20:42.032
[squeals excitedly]

20:42.115 --> 20:44.701
I wanna be the boss's girl so bad.

20:45.202 --> 20:47.037
Hard to pass up Caiman, though.

20:47.120 --> 20:48.205
[Nikaido laughs]

20:50.290 --> 20:52.125
These clothes are weird.

20:52.209 --> 20:54.795
[Natsuki] Ugh, the cross tattoo
is stinging my eye!

20:55.879 --> 20:57.714
[Dokuga] I brought you your food.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.967
[Natsuki] Looks delicious!

21:00.050 --> 21:02.344
[Dokuga] This is complimentary local sake.

21:02.427 --> 21:03.345
[gasps]

21:05.430 --> 21:06.765
[laughter in distance]

21:06.848 --> 21:08.976
[Dokuga] Probably just my imagination...

21:09.059 --> 21:11.478
[Natsuki] Come on, Caiman, one more!

21:13.772 --> 21:15.482
[both laugh triumphantly]

21:15.565 --> 21:17.484
Both of you are drinking too much.

21:17.567 --> 21:19.820
It's fine. Nikaido, you drink too!

21:19.903 --> 21:21.822
Tiny sushi! [giggles]

21:21.905 --> 21:23.323
Nom! So good!

21:23.407 --> 21:25.200
[Nikaido] It looks like
Caiman has cheered up

21:25.284 --> 21:27.160
thanks to the sake and food.

21:27.244 --> 21:28.578
I'm glad.

21:28.662 --> 21:30.289
Caiman, gimmie a kiss!

21:31.081 --> 21:32.249
[screaming]

21:34.584 --> 21:36.128
[Nikaido] Natsuki hasn't noticed

21:36.211 --> 21:39.089
that the crosses
on Caiman's eyes have disappeared.

21:40.507 --> 21:41.591
Huh?

21:41.675 --> 21:43.510
[gentle piano music playing]

21:47.139 --> 21:49.016
[Caiman] Nikaido, what's wrong?

21:49.766 --> 21:51.518
Have another drink with me.

21:51.601 --> 21:53.603
Uh... sure.

21:56.606 --> 21:59.151
You know,
I've been pretty worried about you.

21:59.234 --> 22:02.029
Since we went to the old school,
you've been off.

22:02.112 --> 22:04.448
You're right. Sorry about that.

22:04.948 --> 22:06.033
Hey, Caiman.

22:06.116 --> 22:08.744
If your memories ever do come back,

22:08.827 --> 22:10.662
would you still... want to live

22:10.746 --> 22:14.374
in this world with Natsuki
and your companions as a Cross-Eye?

22:14.875 --> 22:17.544
Uh... Well, I guess I'm not sure,

22:17.627 --> 22:21.882
but for now at the very least,
I plan to go back to the Hole.

22:22.466 --> 22:24.551
Hey, what are you asking me all that for?

22:25.135 --> 22:27.137
Caiman, it's just...

22:27.637 --> 22:30.307
There's something
I've wanted to ask you for a while.

22:31.058 --> 22:33.477
Once you return back to your normal self,

22:33.977 --> 22:35.812
would you mind helping me
at my restaurant?

22:35.896 --> 22:36.813
Huh?

22:36.897 --> 22:38.565
I was going to wait to ask

22:38.648 --> 22:40.817
until your problem
was all straightened out,

22:40.901 --> 22:43.070
but for some reason,

22:43.153 --> 22:46.823
I don't know why, but it feels like
I have to ask you this tonight.

22:47.324 --> 22:49.242
[Caiman] Would you be okay
with someone like me?

22:49.326 --> 22:50.327
[Nikaido gasps]

22:52.412 --> 22:53.580
Yeah.

22:54.122 --> 22:55.332
I could use you, Caiman.

22:55.916 --> 22:57.834
[chuckles] Nikaido...

22:57.918 --> 23:00.253
[Nikaido] Besides,
I'm gonna go out of business

23:00.337 --> 23:01.588
if you stay as a customer.

23:01.671 --> 23:02.506
[Caiman] The hell?!

23:04.257 --> 23:06.510
[Nikaido] In the end,
my feeling was right.

23:07.219 --> 23:08.804
It was good I asked,

23:08.887 --> 23:11.014
because that was the last night

23:11.932 --> 23:14.142
I ever talked with Caiman.

23:15.852 --> 23:17.604
[Japanese theme song playing]

24:43.648 --> 24:44.941
THE END

24:45.025 --> 24:47.486
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 17.

24:47.569 --> 24:49.237
That man's name is Ai.

24:49.321 --> 24:51.114
Ebisu is from a respectable family.

24:51.198 --> 24:53.617
Things are going well
between Caiman and Nikaido.

24:53.700 --> 24:57.454
What we're going to learn in Episode 18,
it's still lost in chaos.

24:57.537 --> 24:59.956
This is Dorohedoro!
